 "problems": [],
 "caption": "\n  \\textbf{ODE trajectory evolution across training iterations}\n  (Colour MNIST-RGB \\emph{simple} experiment).\n  \\emph{Columns} (left $\\to$ right): forward model at different\n  training iterations (Initial $\\to$ Final).\n  \\emph{Rows} (top $\\to$ bottom): ODE time $t$ from source ($t{=}0$)\n  to transported image ($t{=}1$), integrated with 200 Euler steps.\n  The same PURPLE digit-7 source is used in every column.\n  Adaptation progressively tilts the transport from the wrong\n  colour (dark-blue at iteration~0) toward the correct CYAN target,\n  demonstrating cost-free transfer of the cyclic channel-permutation law.",
 "figure_latex": "\\begin{figure}[ht]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{images/paper_grid_figure.pdf}\n\\caption{\n  \\textbf{ODE trajectory evolution across training iterations}\n  (Colour MNIST-RGB \\emph{simple} experiment).\n  \\emph{Columns} (left $\\to$ right): forward model at different\n  training iterations (Initial $\\to$ Final).\n  \\emph{Rows} (top $\\to$ bottom): ODE time $t$ from source ($t{=}0$)\n  to transported image ($t{=}1$), integrated with 200 Euler steps.\n  The same PURPLE digit-7 source is used in every column.\n  Adaptation progressively tilts the transport from the wrong\n  colour (dark-blue at iteration~0) toward the correct CYAN target,\n  demonstrating cost-free transfer of the cyclic channel-permutation law.}\n\\label{fig:color_grid}\n\\end{figure}",
 "title": "Generative Transfer for Entropic Optimal Transport with Unknown Costs",
